# Copper Linux -- the components starthyprland offers before it starts Hyprland.
#
# Three whitespace-separated columns:
#
#   <name>   <probe>                       <how>
#
# <probe> is a path that exists when the component is present. starthyprland
# installs the missing ones whose <how> is "ingot", by asking ingot for them.
# <how> of "image" means the hyprland stage already ships it in the ISO: it is
# kept in this list so the report is honest about what a desktop is supposed to
# have, but ingot has no such package and starthyprland will not try to install
# one -- a missing "image" component is a broken image, said out loud.
#
# The ingot payloads here are the ones copper-ingot-repo carries for every
# desktop (firefox, mousepad, ristretto, xarchiver, htop). They are not needed
# for the session to start, but they work under Wayland and are the ones that
# exist in the repo. Each deb payload carries its full closure, so declining the
# prompt costs nothing and accepting it downloads a few hundred MB; the session
# starts either way.

firefox             /usr/bin/firefox             ingot
mousepad            /usr/bin/mousepad            ingot
ristretto           /usr/bin/ristretto           ingot
xarchiver           /usr/bin/xarchiver           ingot
htop                /usr/bin/htop                ingot

hyprland            /usr/bin/hyprland            image
waybar              /usr/bin/waybar              image
fuzzel              /usr/bin/fuzzel              image
kitty               /usr/bin/kitty               image
hyprlock            /usr/bin/hyprlock            image
hyprpaper           /usr/bin/hyprpaper           image
hypridle            /usr/bin/hypridle            image
hyprpicker          /usr/bin/hyprpicker          image
dunst               /usr/bin/dunst               image
wl-clipboard        /usr/bin/wl-copy             image
cliphist            /usr/bin/cliphist            image
jq                  /usr/bin/jq                  image
brightnessctl       /usr/bin/brightnessctl       image
playerctl           /usr/bin/playerctl           image
